# LOCAL.md

Everything specific to *this* checkout and its owner, split across three gitignored files (may
contain server addresses, names, employers, document ids and anything else you would not
publish):

- **`LOCAL.md`** (this file) - short standing rules and instance config. Read every run.
- **`LOCAL_KNOWLEDGE.md`** - what you know about the owner, their correspondents and recurring
  document patterns, needed to classify new documents correctly. Also read every run.
- **`LOCAL_LOG.md`** - a chronological incident log, one entry per run. NOT read automatically;
  only consult it (grep for a doc id or keyword) when a past incident, bugfix or a specific
  document's history becomes relevant.

Copy the three `*.example` files to drop the `.example` suffix and fill in what you know;
sections you leave empty are fine. Agents read `LOCAL.md` and `LOCAL_KNOWLEDGE.md` after
`AGENTS.md`; rules here override the defaults there. See section 9 in `AGENTS.md` for which of
the three files a new finding belongs in.

## Instance

- Paperless version, reachable URLs (the token itself stays in `.env`).
- Inbox tag name and id.
- Anything unusual about the configuration (duplicate handling, archive generation, ...).

## Conventions on this instance

- Operating mode if not fully automatic (e.g. "ask before apply").
- Document language and title pattern if different from `<What> (<Who>) - DD.MM.YYYY`.
- Name of the duplicate tag (default `Duplikat-Verdacht`).
- Spelling conventions for correspondents and tags (umlauts vs. ASCII, abbreviations).
- Known inconsistencies that must NOT be cleaned up (two tags meaning the same thing, ...).
- Preferred document types and what they cover.

## Machine-specific setup notes

- Where Tesseract/Ghostscript/poppler live, `TESSDATA_PREFIX`, anything that took a while
  to get working.
